<%--
Add_Api_Key_Modal_Form - Modal form for creating API keys

Collects the key name and the key's ACCESS: unrestricted (the key carries every permission
its holder has) or scoped (the key is narrowed to a rule set, and can never reach anything
outside it).

The form declares its endpoint on the <Rsx_Form> tag - the single place the endpoint is
named - and the hosting Modal.form() drives that form's submit(). VALIDATION IS THE
SERVER'S, including every scope rule: create_key canonicalises the union itself and answers
a malformed rule under the `scopes` field. The panel below the fields is a PREVIEW, not a
check - it shows what the rules reach, and it is the same resolver the dispatcher uses.

Keys are immutable after mint: there is no edit form anywhere, because narrowing a
credential already in service would change its meaning under the integration holding it.
Revoke and mint a replacement instead.
--%>
<Define:Add_Api_Key_Modal_Form>

    <Rsx_Form $sid="form" $controller="Frontend_Settings_Api_Keys_Controller" $method="create_key">

        <Form_Errors />

        <Form_Field $label="Key Name" $required=true
            $help="Give your key a descriptive name so you can identify it later.">
            <Text_Input $name="name" $max_length=255 $placeholder="e.g., Production API, CI/CD Integration" $autofocus=true />
        </Form_Field>

        <Form_Field $label="Access" $required=true>
            <Select_With_Description_Input $sid="access_mode" $name="access_mode" $options=this.data.access_options />
        </Form_Field>

        <%-- Present on every render and merely hidden while the key is unrestricted: the
             inputs inside it still serialize, and the server ignores them for an
             unrestricted key. A branch would destroy the operator's half-written rules
             every time they looked at the other mode. --%>
        <div $sid="scoped_section" class="Add_Api_Key_Modal_Form__scoped">

            <Form_Field $label="Presets">
                <Api_Scope_Presets_Input $sid="presets" $name="presets" $options=this.data.presets />
            </Form_Field>

            <Form_Field $label="Custom rules"
                $help="One rule per line: Grant or Deny, a method, and a path pattern - for example Grant POST /api/v1/contacts/*/update. A single star matches exactly one path segment; a double star matches the rest of the path and may only be the last segment. Nothing matched means denied, and a Deny beats a Grant written at the same precision.">
                <Text_Input $sid="custom_rules" $name="scopes" $type="textarea" $rows=4 $max_length=-1
                    $placeholder="Grant GET /api/v1/tasks/**" />
            </Form_Field>

            <Api_Scope_Preview $sid="preview" $scopes="" />

        </div>

    </Rsx_Form>

</Define:Add_Api_Key_Modal_Form>
